# EM Bot — Cursor AI Rules

## Project overview
TypeScript ESM monorepo. Two products:
1. `features/weekly-review` — Tuesday cron bot: reads JIRA Epics, calls Claude via tool-use, posts ADF comments.
2. `features/progress-dashboard` — Multi-tenant SaaS: Next.js 15 frontend on Vercel + Node pipeline on GitHub Actions. EMs sign up, connect JIRA + Anthropic, get a live dashboard. Credentials encrypted in Supabase Vault.

## Language and toolchain
- TypeScript strict mode, ESM (`"type": "module"`), Node 20+
- Path aliases: `@shared/*` → `./shared/*`, `@weekly-review/*` → `./features/weekly-review/*`
- Test: Vitest. Run: `npm test`. 250+ tests, no credentials needed.
- Build: `npm run build`. Typecheck: `npm run typecheck`. Lint: `npm run lint`.
- Frontend: Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, Tailwind CSS

## Code style rules
- No comments unless the WHY is non-obvious (hidden constraint, workaround for a specific bug)
- Never explain what code does — well-named identifiers do that
- No multi-paragraph docstrings or multi-line comment blocks
- No backwards-compat shims, dead code, unused exports
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- No security vulnerabilities: no command injection, XSS, SQL injection
- Validate at system boundaries (user input, external APIs) only
- No hypothetical future-proofing or premature abstractions

## Architecture rules
- JIRA: `POST /rest/api/3/search/jql` cursor-based — does NOT accept `startAt`, use `nextPageToken`
- Supabase: pipeline uses service role key (bypasses RLS); frontend uses anon key. Never swap.
- `next.config.ts` must NOT have `output: 'export'` — server-rendered mode required for Auth
- `EpicSnapshotSchema` field names — any change cascades to snapshotBuilder, promptBuilder, all fixtures, dashboard pipeline
- `AnalysisResultSchema` enum values — must stay in sync with `tool.ts` input_schema and `adfBuilder.ts`
- `DashboardPayload` shape changes need corresponding update to `frontend/lib/types.ts`
- Vault secrets are stored as UUIDs in `tenant_config` — raw API keys never stored in DB columns

## Multi-tenant pipeline (progress-dashboard)
- `TENANT_ID` env var present → `loadConfigFromSupabase(tenantId)` → write to `dashboard_data` table
- `TENANT_ID` absent → load from `dashboard-config.yaml` + `.env` → write to `dashboard.json` (local dev)
- Vault decrypt: `SELECT decrypted_secret FROM vault.decrypted_secrets WHERE id = $1`
- `upsertDashboardData()` writes payload AND updates `next_run_at` in `tenant_config`

## LLM integration (weekly-review)
- Tool: `submit_epic_analysis`. `tool_choice: {type:"tool", name:"submit_epic_analysis"}` always forced.
- On Zod failure: append corrective note to system prompt, retry up to `maxRetries+1` total.
- Wrong `epicKey` in tool response: throw immediately, no retry.

## LLM integration (progress-dashboard)
- Three tools: `submit_team_progress` (1 call), `submit_epic_goal_summary` (per epic), `submit_person_weekly_goal` (per person-epic).
- `analyseTeamProgress` throws `LlmAnalysisFailedError` on exhaustion.
- `analyseEpicGoal` returns fallback object on exhaustion (does not throw).
- `analyseWeeklyGoal` skips LLM entirely when `ownerUpdatesThisWeek.length === 0`.
- Prompts in `src/prompts/*.md` loaded at runtime via `readFileSync` — no rebuild needed.

## Testing patterns
- Mock `fs.readFileSync` for prompt loading in LLM analyser tests
- Mock `@weekly-review/src/jira/snapshotBuilder.js` for epic fetcher tests
- Mock `@supabase/supabase-js` for Supabase loader/writer tests
- LLM mock: create `Anthropic.Message`-shaped objects with `content: [{type:'tool_use', ...}]`
- Never hit real JIRA, Supabase, or Anthropic in tests

## Frontend (features/progress-dashboard/frontend)
- Server Components: use `createServerClient()` from `lib/supabase/server.ts`
- Client Components: use `createBrowserClient()` from `lib/supabase/client.ts`
- API routes: use `createServiceClient()` from `lib/supabase/server.ts` (service role, no cookies)
- Auth middleware in `middleware.ts`: unauth → /login, no onboarding → /onboarding, / → /dashboard
- Env vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`

## Supabase schema
- `tenants`: id (= auth.users.id), org_name, logo_url, brand_color, onboarding_completed_at
- `tenant_config`: tenant_id, jira_base_url, jira_user_email, jira_api_token_secret (UUID), anthropic_key_secret (UUID), project_keys[], schedule_days[], schedule_time_utc, next_run_at, last_run_at
- `dashboard_data`: tenant_id, payload (jsonb), generated_at, run_status (pending|running|success|failed), error_msg
- RLS: `USING (auth.uid() = tenant_id)` on all tables. Service role bypasses RLS.
- Storage bucket: `logos` (public URLs stored in `tenants.logo_url`)

## GitHub Actions secrets
- `em-bot-weekly.yml`: needs JIRA_BASE_URL, JIRA_USER_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
- `progress-dashboard.yml` (meta-runner every 30 min): needs SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY only
